WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
JAMIE: Intel's Ohio plant would
like a word.

00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:03.270
RUFUS: Precisely.

00:00:03.483 --> 00:00:05.213
ALEX: So what's the point of the
presidential visit?

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:06.943
ALEX: Just optics?

00:00:07.028 --> 00:00:09.887
JAMIE: I don't think it's only
optics. There's something

00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:12.746
JAMIE: real in the signal. The
president showing up

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.605
JAMIE: says, with his physical
presence, that this is

00:00:15.605 --> 00:00:18.464
JAMIE: a national priority. That
changes how suppliers, engineers,

00:00:18.464 --> 00:00:21.323
JAMIE: and states compete for the
downstream contracts.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:24.380
RUFUS: And from a capital-
allocation standpoint, two hundred
and

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.327
RUFUS: sixty-five billion dollars
anchoring in the United States

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:30.274
RUFUS: reshapes the geography of
the global semiconductor industry

00:00:30.274 --> 00:00:33.221
RUFUS: over twenty years. That's
not trivial, even if

00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:36.168
RUFUS: it doesn't fix the GPU
shortage in Q1.
